WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:01.191
(gasp)

00:00:01.191 --> 00:00:03.571
- [Jen] I'm gay, I'm sorry.

00:00:03.571 --> 00:00:04.404
- [Niki] Pick him up.

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:05.390
- Stop yelling at me.

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:06.959
- Look at how happy she is.

00:00:06.959 --> 00:00:07.792
(crying)

00:00:07.792 --> 00:00:09.712
- [Jen] Fucking Christ, Niki!

00:00:09.712 --> 00:00:11.699
- [Niki] I don't know what's happening!

00:00:11.699 --> 00:00:12.733
(yelling)

00:00:12.733 --> 00:00:16.316
- Is this is what it's
like to be a parent?

00:00:17.915 --> 00:00:20.186
- We're becoming fathers.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.019
- Ha ha.

00:00:21.019 --> 00:00:21.852
- Ha ha.

00:00:21.852 --> 00:00:22.685
keep singing!

00:00:22.685 --> 00:00:23.518
(laughter)

00:00:23.518 --> 00:00:24.994
- We will have our first baby.

00:00:24.994 --> 00:00:26.236
- These are babies that they use

00:00:26.236 --> 00:00:27.785
for, like, educational purposes.

00:00:27.785 --> 00:00:30.033
So it's gonna function like a baby

00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:32.913
but it looks a little creepy.

00:00:32.913 --> 00:00:34.567
- We're gay but we're not dating.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:35.567
- We're not dating.

00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:36.400
- No.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.824
- I don't know if we're
gonna be friends after this.

00:00:37.824 --> 00:00:39.572
- I think I'm gonna be a great dad,

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.991
like, dream job is dad.

00:00:41.991 --> 00:00:42.983
- Do you want kids?

00:00:42.983 --> 00:00:43.816
- Yeah.

00:00:43.816 --> 00:00:45.248
- I'm the oldest of three siblings.

00:00:45.248 --> 00:00:46.838
- We're definitely gonna be better parents

00:00:46.838 --> 00:00:47.982
than Jen and Niki.

00:00:47.982 --> 00:00:49.798
- We're gonna have this
baby for a weekend.

00:00:49.798 --> 00:00:50.631
Do you have plans?

00:00:50.631 --> 00:00:51.931
- Yeah, smoke weed and cry.

00:00:51.931 --> 00:00:53.795
- We figured out a good
schedule for both of us

00:00:53.795 --> 00:00:54.755
and then on Sunday

00:00:54.755 --> 00:00:56.234
we're just gonna have fun with our baby.

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:57.298
- Yeah, I think I'll be a good mom.

00:00:57.298 --> 00:00:58.506
I just have to marry somebody

00:00:58.506 --> 00:01:01.130
that doesn't have ADHD
and it'll balance out.

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:02.797
- I don't have ADHD.

00:01:06.707 --> 00:01:07.540
- Oh God.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:08.522
- Careful of it's neck.

00:01:08.522 --> 00:01:10.235
- [Jen] Look into his eyes.

00:01:10.235 --> 00:01:11.068
Is he alive?

00:01:11.068 --> 00:01:11.901
- Not yet.

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:13.105
- Don't look at me.

00:01:13.105 --> 00:01:14.807
- Don't put your hand over a baby's face.

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:16.099
- I wanna look away from it.

00:01:16.099 --> 00:01:17.297
- Bart?

00:01:17.297 --> 00:01:18.382
- Okay this is Bart.

00:01:18.382 --> 00:01:20.523
He came right out of my va-jeen-gine.

00:01:20.523 --> 00:01:22.912
- Addison Duggan-Nguyen.

00:01:22.912 --> 00:01:24.089
- Our one condition for the weekend

00:01:24.089 --> 00:01:25.393
is that neither of us is allowed

00:01:25.393 --> 00:01:26.927
to call the other one daddy.

00:01:26.927 --> 00:01:27.760
- Is he alive?

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.000
Oh fuck.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.097
- Back to work.

00:01:30.097 --> 00:01:31.363
- Cool okay.
- [Jen] It's a baby.

00:01:31.363 --> 00:01:32.384
- Well we'll see how this goes.

00:01:32.384 --> 00:01:33.217
- Bye.

00:01:33.217 --> 00:01:35.457
Day one and we are gonna go get dinner

00:01:35.457 --> 00:01:39.198
and my loving baby-mama is
sitting in the backseat,

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:40.458
with a baby!

00:01:40.458 --> 00:01:42.472
- Jameson and I are taking our baby,

00:01:42.472 --> 00:01:45.072
Addison over here to dinner.

00:01:45.072 --> 00:01:46.784
- It's her first time in public.

00:01:46.784 --> 00:01:48.096
- As soon as we get in the drive-thru,

00:01:48.096 --> 00:01:49.061
and have to interact with people,

00:01:49.061 --> 00:01:50.176
he just starts screaming.

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.057
- Screaming.

00:01:51.057 --> 00:01:51.929
(crying)

00:01:51.929 --> 00:01:52.794
- Okay!

00:01:52.794 --> 00:01:54.082
Nothing's happening!

00:01:54.082 --> 00:01:54.915
Well In-N-Out,

00:01:54.915 --> 00:01:56.920
they like come to your
car window to talk to you;

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:57.787
so it's like a person,

00:01:57.787 --> 00:01:58.896
it's not like a box.

00:01:58.896 --> 00:01:59.946
(crying)

00:01:59.946 --> 00:02:03.104
- [Jen] Could I please get
one number two with Coke?

00:02:03.104 --> 00:02:03.937
(crying)

00:02:03.937 --> 00:02:05.041
- I think I fucked him up.

00:02:05.041 --> 00:02:06.652
- Well you must have done something bad.

00:02:06.652 --> 00:02:08.620
- Changed the diaper and everything.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:10.327
All we were doing was
going through a drive-thru,

00:02:10.327 --> 00:02:12.413
which is the easier option
of getting fast-food,

00:02:12.413 --> 00:02:14.303
and it was still really hard.

00:02:14.303 --> 00:02:16.407
- Night one of fatherhood,

00:02:16.407 --> 00:02:18.206
Addison acted up a little bit

00:02:18.206 --> 00:02:19.823
and it's just really hard,

00:02:19.823 --> 00:02:21.614
to listen to a baby cry in the backseat

00:02:21.614 --> 00:02:23.094
and you can't do anything.

00:02:23.094 --> 00:02:24.678
- She just doesn't stop.

00:02:24.678 --> 00:02:28.887
("Dance Of The Sugarplum
Fairy" by Tchaikovsky)

00:02:28.887 --> 00:02:30.391
- [Niki] Rice Ball, do you like him?

00:02:30.391 --> 00:02:31.685
- [Jen] Like the baby Rice Ball?

00:02:31.685 --> 00:02:33.138
- We decided that we were
gonna do a sleep over

00:02:33.138 --> 00:02:33.971
the next night.

00:02:33.971 --> 00:02:34.804
- So Jen left.

00:02:34.804 --> 00:02:35.637
- [Jen] I went home.
- So I had the baby.

00:02:35.637 --> 00:02:37.062
All right, bye Jen.

00:02:37.062 --> 00:02:38.357
- [Jen] Bye Niki, see you tomorrow.

00:02:38.357 --> 00:02:40.255
- [Niki] See you tomorrow.

00:02:40.255 --> 00:02:41.088
- [Jen] Peace!

00:02:41.088 --> 00:02:42.239
- [Niki] Say bye, Bart.

00:02:42.239 --> 00:02:43.886
(door slams)

00:02:43.886 --> 00:02:45.128
(heavy sigh)

00:02:45.128 --> 00:02:46.376
- I started getting really into it,

00:02:46.376 --> 00:02:47.601
without even noticing.

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:49.528
I started caressing
her and then I thought,

00:02:49.528 --> 00:02:50.361
oh my gosh wait,

00:02:50.361 --> 00:02:52.440
this baby isn't a real baby.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.633
Friday night was great,

00:02:53.633 --> 00:02:54.577
super chill.

00:02:54.577 --> 00:02:57.040
Saturday was when like
all hell broke loose.

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:59.123
(crying)

00:03:03.594 --> 00:03:04.427
- [Kevin] No?

00:03:04.427 --> 00:03:05.260
No milk?

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:07.103
Okay.

00:03:07.103 --> 00:03:08.222
My glasses broke in half

00:03:08.222 --> 00:03:10.222
and I went in to Target.

00:03:14.174 --> 00:03:15.636
And of course she wants
her diaper changed,

00:03:15.636 --> 00:03:16.995
so I'm just like, okay,

00:03:16.995 --> 00:03:18.875
clear all the clothes off of the table.

00:03:18.875 --> 00:03:20.195
Everybody's walking around

00:03:20.195 --> 00:03:21.908
and they're like staring at me hardcore,

00:03:21.908 --> 00:03:22.741
and judging me.

00:03:22.741 --> 00:03:23.788
I'm just like, you know what?

00:03:23.788 --> 00:03:25.313
I have a baby I have to take care of.

00:03:25.313 --> 00:03:27.020
And so I change her diaper right there.

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:28.026
- I tell Niki,

00:03:28.026 --> 00:03:29.330
okay, I'm gonna be at your apartment

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:30.801
by like one or 2:30.

00:03:30.801 --> 00:03:32.251
- No, you said like noon.

00:03:32.251 --> 00:03:33.922
- Jen said she had a haircut at 10:30

00:03:33.922 --> 00:03:35.793
and that she'd come by
after to get the baby.

00:03:35.793 --> 00:03:36.664
She just texted me and told me

00:03:36.664 --> 00:03:38.450
her haircut was actually at 1:30,

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.288
so she's not gonna be here until three.

00:03:40.288 --> 00:03:41.352
So while you're gone,

00:03:41.352 --> 00:03:43.808
my sister comes to visit
and we try to go get food.

00:03:43.808 --> 00:03:45.296
The second I step outside the car,

00:03:45.296 --> 00:03:47.269
of course he starts screaming.

00:03:47.269 --> 00:03:48.965
(crying)

00:03:48.965 --> 00:03:51.455
Babies have sensitive necks,

00:03:51.455 --> 00:03:52.288
like real babies,

00:03:52.288 --> 00:03:54.903
so if you put their
necks in weird positions

00:03:54.903 --> 00:03:57.449
they get very upset because
you're mishandling them.

00:03:57.449 --> 00:03:59.626
Okay I think I mishandled him,

00:03:59.626 --> 00:04:01.354
'cause he's screaming really badly.

00:04:01.354 --> 00:04:03.369
(crying)

00:04:03.369 --> 00:04:04.687
I don't know what to do.

00:04:04.687 --> 00:04:05.644
There's only so much I can do,

00:04:05.644 --> 00:04:06.782
I'm one person.

00:04:06.782 --> 00:04:08.214
- It's time for a little quality time,

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:10.350
with me and little Miss Addison.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:13.229
Now I'm gonna try and
cook a meal for myself.

00:04:13.229 --> 00:04:14.062
- I don't know,

00:04:14.062 --> 00:04:16.428
I feel kinda guilty
just leaving her behind.

00:04:16.428 --> 00:04:18.581
Can't wait to be reunited
with my daughter.

00:04:18.581 --> 00:04:21.561
- Right after he gets done screaming,

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:22.700
for like 30 minutes.
- [Jen] I'm the luckiest woman

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:23.783
in the world.

00:04:25.229 --> 00:04:26.421
- He's yours now, take him.

00:04:26.421 --> 00:04:27.657
- He was so calm.

00:04:27.657 --> 00:04:29.084
As soon as I got to Niki's house

00:04:29.084 --> 00:04:30.660
that baby just like did not cry.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:31.780
- Nothing.

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:33.617
- Trying to get ready to
go to a birthday party

00:04:33.617 --> 00:04:35.766
and she decides that she is now hungry.

00:04:35.766 --> 00:04:39.358
I don't know how new parents
can be anywhere on time

00:04:39.358 --> 00:04:42.030
because time really stops
when your baby needs to

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:44.392
eat, or drink, or do anything.

00:04:44.392 --> 00:04:46.976
- We are going to Olive Garden,

00:04:46.976 --> 00:04:48.152
a family restaurant,

00:04:48.152 --> 00:04:49.518
because what a family.

00:04:49.518 --> 00:04:53.874
- We're next to a table
with actual children.

00:04:53.874 --> 00:04:55.082
- He's real narky.

00:04:55.082 --> 00:04:55.915
(laughing)

00:04:55.915 --> 00:04:56.748
- Nothing was happening,

00:04:56.748 --> 00:04:57.581
he was sleeping.

00:04:57.581 --> 00:04:58.600
But I was so anxious just sitting there,

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:01.473
waiting for something to happen.

00:05:01.473 --> 00:05:02.306
He's still hungry,

00:05:02.306 --> 00:05:03.511
he's just being fussy.

00:05:03.511 --> 00:05:06.013
(crying)

00:05:06.013 --> 00:05:07.304
- What is happening?

00:05:07.304 --> 00:05:08.137
- Okay.

00:05:08.137 --> 00:05:09.458
- There was like an element of pride,

00:05:09.458 --> 00:05:11.227
like I am responsible
enough to have a child

00:05:11.227 --> 00:05:13.893
and to have us somewhere where he can sit.

00:05:13.893 --> 00:05:17.085
- When you take a robotic
baby to Dave &amp; Busters,

00:05:17.085 --> 00:05:19.163
prepare to get a lot of stares

00:05:19.163 --> 00:05:20.806
an people judging you

00:05:20.806 --> 00:05:23.076
because they don't understand fatherhood.

00:05:23.076 --> 00:05:25.797
Also, all the minors
had to leave after 10pm

00:05:25.797 --> 00:05:27.732
but since Addison's a robot

00:05:27.732 --> 00:05:29.879
she was allowed to stay.

00:05:29.879 --> 00:05:31.822
- Niki's gonna go to sleep in her room.

00:05:31.822 --> 00:05:33.965
I'mma sleep next to the
little nugget out here

00:05:33.965 --> 00:05:36.950
and if he cries I will start crying,

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:38.958
and that will surely wake Niki up.

00:05:38.958 --> 00:05:41.269
- Around two AM she started crying.

00:05:41.269 --> 00:05:43.068
She wanted to be fed,

00:05:43.068 --> 00:05:44.334
so did that.

00:05:44.334 --> 00:05:46.914
She drank from her bottle
for like 15 minutes

00:05:46.914 --> 00:05:48.465
which doesn't make sense,

00:05:48.465 --> 00:05:49.454
that length of time.

00:05:49.454 --> 00:05:50.287
- Having a child,

00:05:50.287 --> 00:05:51.120
the early years,

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:52.072
is pretty much a guarantee

00:05:52.072 --> 00:05:53.744
you will not get a good
night sleep most of the time.

00:05:53.744 --> 00:05:55.271
- We are on the way,

00:05:55.271 --> 00:05:59.224
to going on a morning stroll with Addison.

00:05:59.224 --> 00:06:01.713
- I'm sure I'll get
emotional on the stroll.

00:06:01.713 --> 00:06:03.065
- [Niki] What time is it Jen?

00:06:03.065 --> 00:06:04.975
- It's 10:54.

00:06:04.975 --> 00:06:06.294
- [Niki] Have you moved
from this couch yet?

00:06:06.294 --> 00:06:07.127
- No.

00:06:07.127 --> 00:06:07.960
- This has been great,

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:09.188
like this has been so much fun.

00:06:09.188 --> 00:06:10.021
I've loved it.

00:06:10.021 --> 00:06:12.116
- Just the idea of not
having Addison anymore

00:06:12.116 --> 00:06:13.206
(laughing)
kinda scares me.

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:16.145
(lighthearted music)

00:06:16.145 --> 00:06:18.408
(laughing)

00:06:18.408 --> 00:06:19.489
(crying)

00:06:19.489 --> 00:06:20.615
(heaving sighing)

00:06:20.615 --> 00:06:21.595
- Anyways, one day we met up

00:06:21.595 --> 00:06:24.782
with Jameson and Kevin for bunch.

00:06:24.782 --> 00:06:25.880
- Whooo!

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:26.886
Bye baby.

00:06:26.886 --> 00:06:27.719
I think, if anything,

00:06:27.719 --> 00:06:31.285
I just learned that like
doing it for like two days,

00:06:31.285 --> 00:06:32.917
at a very easy level,

00:06:32.917 --> 00:06:34.094
was frustrating.

00:06:34.094 --> 00:06:35.527
So it's like the fact that you can do it

00:06:35.527 --> 00:06:38.127
for the rest of your life is impressive.

00:06:38.127 --> 00:06:39.654
So thank you moms and dads.

00:06:39.654 --> 00:06:40.597
- Sorry Mom.

00:06:40.597 --> 00:06:42.693
- I thought it was like
pretty good and responsible

00:06:42.693 --> 00:06:43.870
but at the same time it's like,

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:44.742
it's a handful.

00:06:44.742 --> 00:06:45.575
Because you don't realize it

00:06:45.575 --> 00:06:46.878
until you're actually in it,

00:06:46.878 --> 00:06:47.711
that you're doing it,

00:06:47.711 --> 00:06:48.544
that you're like

00:06:48.544 --> 00:06:49.781
oh my gosh this is what parents do.

00:06:49.781 --> 00:06:50.887
It's like a second job,

00:06:50.887 --> 00:06:52.438
having like a kid.

00:06:52.438 --> 00:06:54.376
- So the babies have
like a computer inside,

00:06:54.376 --> 00:06:56.686
that monitors like your response time;

00:06:56.686 --> 00:06:58.430
it monitors how much
you take care of them;

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:00.163
it can tell if they've been mishandled.

00:07:00.163 --> 00:07:01.534
- Addison knows we love her.

00:07:01.534 --> 00:07:04.262
- I totally think that we
did better than Jen and Niki.

00:07:04.262 --> 00:07:05.727
- Yeah, I think they're
gonna do a better score

00:07:05.727 --> 00:07:06.685
just because it seemed like

00:07:06.685 --> 00:07:08.357
they actually fell in love with their kid.

00:07:08.357 --> 00:07:09.439
- Yeah, they like cared.

00:07:09.439 --> 00:07:10.432
- What did we get?

00:07:10.432 --> 00:07:11.265
C plus?

00:07:11.265 --> 00:07:12.205
(laughing)

00:07:12.205 --> 00:07:13.415
- [Narrator] An 86.

00:07:13.415 --> 00:07:14.541
- What?

00:07:14.541 --> 00:07:15.374
- That's a B.

00:07:15.374 --> 00:07:16.650
- That's a solid B.

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:17.492
- We got a B?

00:07:17.492 --> 00:07:18.616
- Parenting.

00:07:18.616 --> 00:07:19.449
(claps)

00:07:19.449 --> 00:07:21.681
- [Narrator] You guys scored 47%.

00:07:21.681 --> 00:07:22.514
(record scratches)

00:07:22.514 --> 00:07:23.347
- What?

00:07:23.347 --> 00:07:24.180
- That's not possible.

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:25.013
- No way.

00:07:25.013 --> 00:07:27.400
- There's literally no
way that that's possible.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:29.677
- 47 out of a hundred?

00:07:29.677 --> 00:07:32.710
- What did Jen and Niki get?

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:33.913
- [Narrator] 86%.

00:07:33.913 --> 00:07:34.746
(paper crumpling)

00:07:34.746 --> 00:07:35.653
- Shut up!

00:07:35.653 --> 00:07:37.232
That's not possible!

00:07:37.232 --> 00:07:38.065
(laughter)

00:07:38.065 --> 00:07:38.898
We love our baby!

00:07:38.898 --> 00:07:41.188
- We got an 86 and they got an F?

00:07:41.188 --> 00:07:43.272
- Honestly thought we'd
come out at the bottom,

00:07:43.272 --> 00:07:44.105
on this one.

00:07:44.105 --> 00:07:45.948
- I refuse, I refuse to believe this.

00:07:45.948 --> 00:07:47.031
I'm gonna leave now.

00:07:47.031 --> 00:07:48.106
- Good job buddy.

00:07:48.106 --> 00:07:48.939
- [Niki] We did it.

00:07:48.939 --> 00:07:49.846
- We did it.

00:07:49.846 --> 00:07:51.446
(claps)
And we stayed friends.

00:07:51.446 --> 00:07:53.515
- This is why you can't measure parenting.

00:07:53.515 --> 00:07:54.606
- Yeah, you can't measure it.

00:07:54.606 --> 00:07:55.843
I know I'm gonna be a good parent.

00:07:55.843 --> 00:07:56.676
- We did it.

00:07:56.676 --> 00:07:58.171
- We did it!

00:07:58.171 --> 00:07:59.004
- Yes.

00:07:59.004 --> 00:08:00.445
- Have a good weekend.

